            <ArticleTitle>Nineteen-year-old female with unilateral ankle pain. What is your diagnosis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>74-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case history of a 19-year-old female with left ankle pain of 18 months' duration is presented. The reader is encouraged to make his or her own diagnosis after reviewing the history, laboratory values, and imaging. The final diagnosis with a full explanation and differential diagnosis will follow.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
